%% Card authorisation — the hot path
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant M as Merchant / Acquirer
    participant S as Scheme
    participant P as Issuer-processor
    participant D as Decisioning
    participant F as Feature store
    participant L as Ledger
    M->>S: Authorisation request
    S->>P: ISO 8583 / API
    P->>D: Risk check (latency budget)
    D->>F: Fetch features (JIT + cached)
    F-->>D: Features
    D-->>P: approve / decline / step-up
    P->>L: Idempotent hold
    L-->>P: OK / insufficient funds
    P-->>S: Response
    S-->>M: Approved
    Note over P,L: Stand-in policy if ledger unavailable —<br/>limits and exposure owner must be explicit
    P->>L: Clearing & settlement (T+n)
